                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5ea2f716-4c22-3af3-980e-2d54151bb9ae",
                        "entry_id": "08feaa62-67d3-30a0-8428-510cb3c6dfa1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "действовать быстрее кого-либо или чего-либо"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0a3aa280-e2db-4a3a-81d5-67f8c32e27a0",
                                "sense_id": "5ea2f716-4c22-3af3-980e-2d54151bb9ae",
                                "text": "Может быть, эта обидчивость у него явилась из досады, что майор и в этом вопросе упредил его, отказавшись от денег заранее, но так или иначе, разговор этот мне пришлось прекратить."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7eb0bdef-396f-3218-bfab-6df1a6daf69b",
                        "entry_id": "08feaa62-67d3-30a0-8428-510cb3c6dfa1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар. то же, что предупреждать"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1d17517d-c7c3-4a5e-a7b4-38b81a733920",
                                "sense_id": "7eb0bdef-396f-3218-bfab-6df1a6daf69b",
                                "text": "Но в высылке этих машин и инженера вышло какое-то qui pro quo: машины запоздали и пришли очень поздно, а инженер упредил наши ожидания и приехал в Петербург раньше времени."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6446e2a0-64fe-4d21-aba1-5345a8c05c5b",
                        "source_entry_id": "08feaa62-67d3-30a0-8428-510cb3c6dfa1",
                        "target_lang_word": "forestall",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "forestall",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "341b2a79-906c-3ebc-8b7f-aa715a408955",
                                        "entry_id": "1c491d2a-4514-37af-8844-c93b2900e86d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To prevent, delay or hinder something by taking precautionary or anticipatory measures; to avert."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "518115f9-8799-4111-a263-24faa6eb0c96",
                                                "sense_id": "341b2a79-906c-3ebc-8b7f-aa715a408955",
                                                "text": "Fred forestalled disaster by his prompt action."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f3aa8a8-4728-41ac-8661-a623e29620ab",
                                                "sense_id": "341b2a79-906c-3ebc-8b7f-aa715a408955",
                                                "text": "The Act of 1846 also authorised a branch from the village of Broughty Ferry on the D. & A. to the pier at Broughty Ferry Castle. This action was taken to forestall the Edinburgh & Northern Railway, which had acquired the ferry between Ferryport-on-Craig (Tayport from July, 1851) and Broughty Ferry, and had hopes of a connecting railway on the north side of the Tay."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c38ca180-24f4-3c49-b7db-14009a334611",
                                        "entry_id": "1c491d2a-4514-37af-8844-c93b2900e86d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To preclude or bar from happening, render impossible."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e46aeb3d-e62a-4995-8b90-b8c474249f66",
                                                "sense_id": "c38ca180-24f4-3c49-b7db-14009a334611",
                                                "text": "In French, an aspired h forestalls elision."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6fe2aace-c475-3bf0-93d9-a58180f87b3a",
                                        "entry_id": "1c491d2a-4514-37af-8844-c93b2900e86d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To purchase the complete supply of a good, particularly foodstuffs, in order to charge a monopoly price."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1c495fc3-6e4f-3df3-90ea-99b603fe988b",
                                        "entry_id": "1c491d2a-4514-37af-8844-c93b2900e86d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To anticipate, to act foreseeingly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8cfdc258-eb36-4518-a52d-c8a8bc7a7948",
                                                "sense_id": "1c495fc3-6e4f-3df3-90ea-99b603fe988b",
                                                "text": "What need a man forestall his date of grief, / And run to meet what he would most avoid?",
                                                "translation": "Comus",
                                                "english": "Comus"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a50c4ff8-88b1-4aaa-8fb3-da60bbf0b8c5",
                                                "sense_id": "1c495fc3-6e4f-3df3-90ea-99b603fe988b",
                                                "text": "She insisted on doing her share of the offices needful to the sick. She arranged his bed so that it was possible to change the sheet without disturbing him. She washed him. […] She did not speak to him much, but she was quick to forestall his wants."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2da0a586-919d-36d4-ab19-cb6ba1c31d6d",
                                        "entry_id": "1c491d2a-4514-37af-8844-c93b2900e86d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To deprive (with of)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "58882aa4-00a2-4ec0-8d6c-07d07a423c6c",
                                                "sense_id": "2da0a586-919d-36d4-ab19-cb6ba1c31d6d",
                                                "text": "All the better; may / This night forestall him of the coming day!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b0e22056-fe18-3a8b-8a46-a0629248fb8f",
                                        "entry_id": "1c491d2a-4514-37af-8844-c93b2900e86d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To obstruct or stop up, as a road; to stop the passage of a highway; to intercept on the road, as goods on the way to market."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "forestall",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ae1476d1-acdf-341e-9d49-1bdfe98796c1",
                                        "entry_id": "70c8d78f-cc34-3dbe-8cbf-53c2c3ad173a",
